    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1133">

                <pb facs="1647" n="1631" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1631"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.00/4–849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Legation in Syria
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-25T15:00:00-04:00">April 25, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">
                        niact
                    </hi>
                </p>
                <p>174. Pursuant to authority reed from Pres. you are instructed after coordinating
                    arrangements with Brit and Fr colleagues send to Syrian FonOff on Tues Apr 26 or soonest thereafter a
                    note ack[nowledging] <pb facs="1648" n="1632" xml:id="pg1632"/> those recd by
                    Leg urtels 215 Apr 8 and 234 Apr 19.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d1133-f1"/> Fol is suggested draft:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“The Amer Leg presents its compliments to the Syrian Ministry for FonAff and,
                        pursuant to instrs from the United States Government, has the honor to
                        acknowledge the receipt of the Ministry’s note no. S–4 dated April 7, 1949,
                        transmitting a copy of the communiqué issued by the General Command of the
                        Army and Armed Forces in regard to the factors that led to the recent <hi
                            rendition="#italic">coup d’état</hi> in Syria, as well as of the
                        Ministry’s note no. M–6 dated April 18, 1949, informing the Leg that a new
                        Cabinet had been formed and giving the names of the members of the
                        Cabinet.</p>
                    <p>The Leg has been instructed to inform the Ministry that the United States
                        Govt has noted with satisfaction the public assurances which His Excellency
                        the PriMin, Colonel Husni Zaim, has made
                        affirming the intention of the new Syrian Govt to discharge Syria’s
                        obligations arising out of all treaties and internatl agreements entered
                        into by previous Syrian govts, as well as its attachment to democratic
                        principles and its intention to hold new elections at an early date.</p>
                    <p>The Leg avails itself of this opportunity to renew to the Ministry the
                        assurances of its highest consideration.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Tel urgently date note delivered.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1133-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1133-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1133-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1133-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1133-f2-content"> This telegram was repeated to
                London and Paris; copies were sent by air to other Arab capitals, Jerusalem, and Tel
                Aviv. <p>Damascus reported, on April 27, that after coordinating with British and
                    French diplomatic representatives, a note “comprising verbatim text suggested in
                        Deptel 174, April 25, delivered Foreign
                    Office 11 o’clock this morning” (telegram 246, 890D.01/4–2749).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
